---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { legal } from '../data/legal';

/**
 * Data deletion instructions — the URL given to Meta as the app's "Data
 * deletion instructions URL" (App settings › Basic). Meta accepts a page that
 * tells a person how to have their data deleted, in place of a callback
 * endpoint, so this page is that instruction and nothing else.
 *
 * Facebook and Instagram come first because this is what Meta's reviewers
 * open; YouTube and TikTok follow so one page answers the question for every
 * platform Tamtree connects to. The privacy policy's #data-deletion section
 * links here.
 */
const { contactEmail } = legal;
const mail = `mailto:${contactEmail}`;

const sections = [
  { id: 'what-we-hold', title: 'What Tamtree holds' },
  { id: 'in-tamtree', title: 'Delete it in Tamtree' },
  { id: 'facebook-instagram', title: 'Remove access on Facebook and Instagram' },
  { id: 'other-platforms', title: 'YouTube and TikTok' },
  { id: 'by-email', title: 'Ask us to delete it' },
  { id: 'what-happens', title: 'What happens next' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Data deletion"
  description="How to delete the data Tamtree holds from your Facebook, Instagram, YouTube or TikTok connection, or your whole Tamtree account."
  sections={sections}
>
  <p>
    This page explains how to delete the data Tamtree holds because you connected a Facebook Page,
    an Instagram account, a YouTube channel or a TikTok account to it, and how to delete your whole
    Tamtree account. You can do it yourself in a few clicks, or ask us to do it for you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-hold">What Tamtree holds</h2>
  <p>For a connected Facebook Page and Instagram professional account, Tamtree stores:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the access token you provided, encrypted;</li>
    <li>your Facebook Page ID, and the ID of the Instagram account linked to it;</li>
    <li>
      a record of the Reels Tamtree uploaded for you: their IDs, captions, and when they were sent.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Tamtree does not read or store your posts, messages, followers, comments or insights. For
    YouTube and TikTok it holds the equivalent: an encrypted access token, the connected account's
    basic identifiers, and a record of the videos it uploaded. The{' '}
    <a href="/privacy/#connected-accounts">privacy policy</a> has the detail.
  </p>

  <h2 id="in-tamtree">Delete it in Tamtree</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in to Tamtree and open <strong>Credentials</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Find the connection (for example <em>Meta (Facebook Page &amp; Instagram)</em>) and choose
      <strong>Delete</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The stored token and account IDs are deleted immediately, and Tamtree can no longer reach the
    account. Workflows that used the connection will stop at that step until you connect an account
    again.
  </p>

  <h2 id="facebook-instagram">Remove access on Facebook and Instagram</h2>
  <p>
    Deleting the connection in Tamtree removes our copy. To also cancel the access on Meta's side:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>If you created a System User token</strong> (the setup the Tamtree guide describes):
      in <a href="https://business.facebook.com/settings" rel="noopener">Meta Business settings</a>,
      go to <em>Users › System users</em>, select the system user, and choose{' '}
      <strong>Revoke tokens</strong>. To remove the app from your business entirely, open{' '}
      <em>Accounts › Apps</em> and remove it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>If you connected through Facebook Login:</strong> on Facebook, go to{' '}
      <em>Settings &amp; privacy › Settings › Business integrations</em> (or{' '}
      <em>Apps and websites</em>), select the app, and choose <strong>Remove</strong>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Removing access does not delete Reels already published to your Page or Instagram account.
    Delete those on Facebook or Instagram.
  </p>

  <h2 id="other-platforms">YouTube and TikTok</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>YouTube:</strong> delete the connection in Tamtree as above, then remove Tamtree under{' '}
      <em>Third-party apps &amp; services</em> on your{' '}
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google Account</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>TikTok:</strong> delete the connection in Tamtree as above, then remove the app in
      the TikTok app under <em>Settings and privacy › Security › Apps and services</em>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="by-email">Ask us to delete it</h2>
  <p>
    If you cannot sign in, or want your whole Tamtree account deleted, email{' '}
    <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a> from the address on your account (or the one you joined the
    waitlist with) with the subject <strong>Data deletion request</strong>. Tell us which
    connections or which account the request covers. If your request is about a Facebook Page or
    Instagram account, include the Page name or Instagram username.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-happens">What happens next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We confirm we received your request within 7 days.</li>
    <li>
      We complete the deletion within 30 days, and then email you to confirm it is done, with a
      reference you can quote if you contact us about it again.
    </li>
    <li>
      If we need to verify that the request comes from you, we will ask before deleting anything.
    </li>
    <li>
      If the law requires us to keep a record, such as a billing record, we keep only that and tell
      you what was kept.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Legal>
